		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3090&amp;p=24755#p24755"><![CDATA[
Translates to <br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello! I have an HT RD5r with OpenGd77 installed, latest stable version.<br>I'm encountering the following problem:<br>When I program the HT to Operate via Hotspot the radio transmits and receives normally, however when I program it for a local repeater it does not transmit or receive (I see that there is a signal arriving at the Bargrafh) however there is no reception and when I transmit there is no connection to the repeater (Timeout). All TGs, CC, Time Slots and frequencies are within the parameters (I even did a test with another HT DM1701 with its original firmware and it works perfectly.<br>Another curiosity... when I put the RD5R to operate in a scanner I normally receive DMR signals from other services...<br><br>I don't know if it's a problem related to the updated firmware... I wanted to do a test with older firmware but I'm not finding it... I don't know if any comrades had this problem with their radio, but here is my post and a possible help: D</div></blockquote><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Aug 02, 2023 3:57 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
